<title>USA: CBOE to trade Molex, Nationwide Financial options.</title>
<headline>CBOE to trade Molex, Nationwide Financial options.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board Options Exchange said Friday it would list options on Class A shares of Molex Inc on June 11 and on shares of Nationwide Financial Services Inc on June 13.</p>
<p>Molex options will have opening strike prices of 30, 35 and 40 and initial expirations in July, August, October and January. Option Resource Group has been named designated primary market maker (DPM).</p>
<p>For Nationwide Financial, opening strikes will be 25, 30 and 35, with initial expirations in July, August, October and January. LETCO has been named DPM.</p>
<p>((--Derivatives desk, 312 408 8750))</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
